WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.367 --> 00:00:03.100
-You look stunning.
Welcome back to the show.

00:00:03.100 --> 00:00:05.701
-Thank you.
-Rina, we were your first show

00:00:05.701 --> 00:00:07.734
where you made your music debut.
-Yes.

00:00:07.734 --> 00:00:09.200
-That was your first
late-night show.

00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:10.501
Which -- Yeah, we all know you.
We love you.

00:00:10.501 --> 00:00:11.934
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:11.934 --> 00:00:15.067
But now this is your first
late-night talk-show interview.

00:00:15.067 --> 00:00:16.601
-Crazy.
-I'm also your first.

00:00:16.601 --> 00:00:18.200
-Crazy! I love it!
-We're in the history books.

00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:21.334
I'm honored. I'm honored
to be in the history books.

00:00:21.334 --> 00:00:24.334
This is also your first film.
-Yes.

00:00:24.334 --> 00:00:27.234
-Which I almost can't believe
that's real that I'm saying that

00:00:27.234 --> 00:00:28.634
because you're phenomenal
in this film.

00:00:28.634 --> 00:00:31.133
-Oh, my God. Thank you.
I can't believe it, either.

00:00:31.133 --> 00:00:32.601
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:32.601 --> 00:00:34.167
-You're -- I mean,
it's a giant --

00:00:34.167 --> 00:00:36.667
Do you get nervous
when you're doing a film

00:00:36.667 --> 00:00:39.467
as opposed to performing live
as a -- as a musician?

00:00:39.467 --> 00:00:41.934
-Oh, I -- It is a completely
different experience.

00:00:41.934 --> 00:00:43.100
-Different animal.

00:00:43.100 --> 00:00:44.367
-I don't really get nervous
before shows.

00:00:44.367 --> 00:00:46.300
-You don't?
-No.

00:00:46.300 --> 00:00:48.501
I get very excited,
but it's not nerves.

00:00:48.501 --> 00:00:50.701
-Well, how about this?
Look at this show right here.

00:00:50.701 --> 00:00:53.067
This is Tokyo Garden Theater.
Look at how many people.

00:00:53.067 --> 00:00:55.834
-Yes.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:55.834 --> 00:00:57.968
-You're not --
You don't get nervous for that?

00:00:57.968 --> 00:01:01.667
-Past, like, 3,000 people,
I feel like -- the human eye,

00:01:01.667 --> 00:01:03.367
you can't really understand
what's going on.

00:01:03.367 --> 00:01:05.100
You know what I mean.
Do you know what I mean?

00:01:05.100 --> 00:01:06.767
-That's very interesting.
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:01:06.767 --> 00:01:08.767
Yeah, after a certain amount,
you're like, "Who cares?

00:01:08.767 --> 00:01:10.234
3,000 -- 3 million."

00:01:10.234 --> 00:01:11.767
-No, it's -- You --
-No, in a good way.

00:01:11.767 --> 00:01:13.133
-No, I still
can't understand it.

00:01:13.133 --> 00:01:14.300
-You can't see further
than that?

00:01:14.300 --> 00:01:15.701
-Yes.
-When I did stand-up --

00:01:15.701 --> 00:01:17.934
This is back in the day and
people were allowed to smoke

00:01:17.934 --> 00:01:19.601
in stand-up -- in comedy clubs.

00:01:19.601 --> 00:01:21.534
And so it was
all smoke and lights.

00:01:21.534 --> 00:01:23.400
So all you saw were maybe...
-Two people.

00:01:23.400 --> 00:01:24.934
-...a row, two people, yeah.
-Yeah.

00:01:24.934 --> 00:01:26.100
-And I was like,
"Oh, I can do this."

00:01:26.100 --> 00:01:28.200
-Right. Yeah.
-Then they banned smoking,

00:01:28.200 --> 00:01:30.000
and all of a sudden, like,
"There's all these people here?"

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:31.968
Like -- This is like --
"Wow. I don't want to do this.

00:01:31.968 --> 00:01:33.501
This is crazy."
-Bring in the haze.

00:01:33.501 --> 00:01:35.734
-Yeah. "I want the haze."
You want that, yeah.

00:01:35.734 --> 00:01:38.267
But this is --
this is a giant thing.

00:01:38.267 --> 00:01:40.734
You're opposite Keanu Reeves.
-Yeah.

00:01:40.734 --> 00:01:42.200
-When you're in and you're --

00:01:42.200 --> 00:01:44.167
Dude, you carry the film
with Keanu, right?

00:01:44.167 --> 00:01:46.367
I mean, you're amazing in it.
Do you get -- Was he --

00:01:46.367 --> 00:01:47.767
What was he like
when you get there?

00:01:47.767 --> 00:01:49.701
Are you like, "Oh, I just don't
want to flub my lines.

00:01:49.701 --> 00:01:51.167
I want to do..."
-Yeah, I mean --

00:01:51.167 --> 00:01:53.167
So, we had, like,
five weeks of training

00:01:53.167 --> 00:01:54.634
before the five weeks
of shooting,

00:01:54.634 --> 00:01:56.467
which is all at nighttime,
by the way.

00:01:56.467 --> 00:01:57.901
So it's -- Yeah.

00:01:57.901 --> 00:02:01.133
Oh, I mean, if you see any of
the action scenes in the movies,

00:02:01.133 --> 00:02:03.300
they're usually shot
1:00 a.m. to 5:00 a.m.

00:02:03.300 --> 00:02:04.667
-Is that right?
-Yeah.

00:02:04.667 --> 00:02:06.334
-So, what's your
sleep schedule like?

00:02:06.334 --> 00:02:09.334
-It's 8:00 a.m. to 1:00 p.m.

00:02:09.334 --> 00:02:11.367
-Wow. So you're a vampire.
-Yeah. Honestly.

00:02:11.367 --> 00:02:13.367
We'd be wearing sunglasses
on the way home

00:02:13.367 --> 00:02:14.868
so we wouldn't get any sunlight.

00:02:14.868 --> 00:02:15.968
-Wow.
-Yeah.

00:02:15.968 --> 00:02:17.634
And all of our skin
went a bit gray.

00:02:17.634 --> 00:02:18.767
-It did?
-It's not --

00:02:18.767 --> 00:02:20.601
Like, you know,
you're climatized to it.

00:02:20.601 --> 00:02:22.200
You try and, you know,
adjust your sleep schedule.

00:02:22.200 --> 00:02:24.534
But you need vitamin D.
Like, everyone goes a bit crazy.

00:02:24.534 --> 00:02:26.300
-But you look so --
Everyone looks so cool.

00:02:26.300 --> 00:02:28.434
It's so stylized,
and the movie is awesome.

00:02:28.434 --> 00:02:29.901
I mean, yeah,
you know the "John Wick" --

00:02:29.901 --> 00:02:31.834
If you haven't seen it.
But it has everything.

00:02:31.834 --> 00:02:33.601
The lighting,
the direction is so good.

00:02:33.601 --> 00:02:35.701
-Oh, it's amazing. Yeah.
-How did the director know

00:02:35.701 --> 00:02:37.234
that you were right
for this part?

00:02:37.234 --> 00:02:40.133
-Oh, my -- So, it's honestly
like a Hollywood miracle,

00:02:40.133 --> 00:02:42.300
like, fairy-tale story.
-I love these stories.

00:02:42.300 --> 00:02:46.434
-So, basically,
I had just finished writing

00:02:46.434 --> 00:02:49.133
my second album, not fully,
but the bulk of it.

00:02:49.133 --> 00:02:51.300
And I was -- I was having
a creative block before that.

00:02:51.300 --> 00:02:53.467
So it was like kind of --
It was amazing that I met --

00:02:53.467 --> 00:02:55.367
I managed to write most of it
in two months.

00:02:55.367 --> 00:02:58.701
And never in my schedule have
I ever had a couple months free.

00:02:58.701 --> 00:03:00.667
But because I had finished
that block of work,

00:03:00.667 --> 00:03:02.834
there was a couple month free
after that.

00:03:02.834 --> 00:03:06.200
And then I just randomly get
a call from Chad Stahelski.

00:03:06.200 --> 00:03:08.033
He wants to speak with me.

00:03:08.033 --> 00:03:09.901
I'm like, "Why the [bleep]
does he want to speak to me?"

00:03:09.901 --> 00:03:11.901
[ Laughter ]
-Okay.

00:03:11.901 --> 00:03:13.734
-Why does director of "John
Wick" want to speak with me for?

00:03:13.734 --> 00:03:15.234
-Yeah.
-Right?

00:03:15.234 --> 00:03:17.200
-I would think, "Great."
I would take the call.

00:03:17.200 --> 00:03:18.901
-I took the call.
-Yeah.

00:03:18.901 --> 00:03:20.000
-Yeah.
-You go, "What's your problem?"

00:03:20.000 --> 00:03:21.501
-And then he was like --
Yeah. Yeah.

00:03:21.501 --> 00:03:22.934
"What do you want?
What do you want?"

00:03:22.934 --> 00:03:24.767
So, I spoke with him,
and he was like,

00:03:24.767 --> 00:03:26.701
"So, I've been trying
to cast this role."

00:03:26.701 --> 00:03:29.133
And he described the character.

00:03:29.133 --> 00:03:31.701
And, "What are you doing
for the next three months?"

00:03:31.701 --> 00:03:33.801
-That -- Just like that?
-Just like that.

00:03:33.801 --> 00:03:36.234
-But did he know that you --
you can fight and --

00:03:36.234 --> 00:03:40.534
and kick and run around and flip
and roll and shoot arrows?

00:03:40.534 --> 00:03:43.167
-He didn't, and I didn't.
-Okay, perfect.

00:03:43.167 --> 00:03:45.267
Alright. Good.
-So...

00:03:45.267 --> 00:03:47.200
But you know what?
There was a conspiracy.

00:03:47.200 --> 00:03:48.701
-Uh-huh.
-It was my conspiracy.

00:03:48.701 --> 00:03:51.734
Because I'd -- So, I co-direct
some of my videos,

00:03:51.734 --> 00:03:53.400
and I write some of my videos,
as well.

00:03:53.400 --> 00:03:56.601
So, I wrote into my videos
the fact that I'll be, like,

00:03:56.601 --> 00:03:58.701
acting as a character,
so there's a video called "XS"

00:03:58.701 --> 00:04:00.434
where I'm acting like a robot

00:04:00.434 --> 00:04:02.200
and I'm breaking down.
-Yeah.

00:04:02.200 --> 00:04:04.400
-And there's a -- there's
a video called "Bad Friend"

00:04:04.400 --> 00:04:06.300
where I'm looking like
a Japanese salary man

00:04:06.300 --> 00:04:08.133
and doing a fight scene.
-Yeah.

00:04:08.133 --> 00:04:10.701
-Honestly, I was thinking,
"You know what?

00:04:10.701 --> 00:04:13.400
If I've got this budget
to do a music video,

00:04:13.400 --> 00:04:15.234
I'm going to also make it
my acting portfolio."

00:04:15.234 --> 00:04:16.667
-Yeah. Yeah.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:16.667 --> 00:04:20.400
"I'm gonna get..."
Smart. So smart.

00:04:20.400 --> 00:04:22.000
-And it worked!

00:04:22.000 --> 00:04:24.167
Because he said, "I've been
watching your videos.

00:04:24.167 --> 00:04:25.534
Keanu and I watched

00:04:25.534 --> 00:04:27.434
your 'Bad Friend' video
and 'XS' video

00:04:27.434 --> 00:04:29.634
and was so impressed because
clearly you do stunts."

00:04:29.634 --> 00:04:31.133
Because I did fighting
in "Bad Friend."

00:04:31.133 --> 00:04:33.033
-Yeah.
-"And clearly you can act

00:04:33.033 --> 00:04:35.000
in 'XS.'"
-Yeah.

00:04:35.000 --> 00:04:37.367
And you're -- you're funny in
some of your videos, as well.

00:04:37.367 --> 00:04:38.467
-Thank you.

00:04:38.467 --> 00:04:39.834
-Which that'll be the next movie
you do.

00:04:39.834 --> 00:04:42.067
You'll do a comedy.
-Oh, that would be sick.

00:04:42.067 --> 00:04:43.601
It's hard, though.
Comedy's hard.

00:04:43.601 --> 00:04:45.467
-Nah.
-"Eh."

00:04:45.467 --> 00:04:48.100
[ Laughter ]

00:04:48.100 --> 00:04:50.901
-You crush it so awesomely
in this.

00:04:50.901 --> 00:04:54.300
You're coming out -- Again,
bow and arrow, bow and arrow,

00:04:54.300 --> 00:04:56.133
flipping, rolling,
kicking, everything,

00:04:56.133 --> 00:04:57.634
then use the arrow.
-Yeah.

00:04:57.634 --> 00:04:59.601
-Stabbing people with
your arrow -- your bow.

00:04:59.601 --> 00:05:00.868
-Yep, doing splits.

00:05:00.868 --> 00:05:03.300
-How much training goes
into all this stuff?

00:05:03.300 --> 00:05:05.200
'Cause it's you, right?
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:05:05.200 --> 00:05:06.968
It was five weeks of training.
-Yeah.

00:05:06.968 --> 00:05:09.767
-Which is not enough.
-No.

00:05:09.767 --> 00:05:12.334
-And then the first week,
they were like,

00:05:12.334 --> 00:05:14.100
"Oh, we're just
going to do some drills

00:05:14.100 --> 00:05:15.701
just to get you warmed up."
-Yeah.

00:05:15.701 --> 00:05:17.300
-And I --
I think it was honestly

00:05:17.300 --> 00:05:18.901
the first day of training.

00:05:18.901 --> 00:05:21.067
I did a move that we --
You just dodge underneath.

00:05:21.067 --> 00:05:23.434
Like, you're in a squat position
and you just dodge like this.

00:05:23.434 --> 00:05:25.234
-Yeah, that's it.
-And then like this.

00:05:25.234 --> 00:05:27.701
-Yeah, I would throw my back out
and be out...

00:05:27.701 --> 00:05:30.467
-Okay. Listen.
So, I threw my back out.

00:05:30.467 --> 00:05:32.934
[ Laughter ]

00:05:32.934 --> 00:05:34.467
-Guy's like, "Who cast her?"
-First day.

00:05:34.467 --> 00:05:35.868
-Yeah. First day?
-Yeah, first day.

00:05:35.868 --> 00:05:37.200
-So you don't tell anybody,
right?

00:05:37.200 --> 00:05:38.434
-How embarr--
No, I didn't tell anyone.

00:05:38.434 --> 00:05:40.200
-Of course not.
-So, I pinched I nerve.

00:05:40.200 --> 00:05:43.167
So, I don't know if anyone
has pinched a nerve before.

00:05:43.167 --> 00:05:44.901
Well, it does --
-It's terrible.

00:05:44.901 --> 00:05:47.234
-It grabs the muscles
around your nerve,

00:05:47.234 --> 00:05:49.434
and it shrinks it.

00:05:49.434 --> 00:05:51.234
So, I was trying to hide it.

00:05:51.234 --> 00:05:54.434
But after a couple of days, my
spine started going like this.

00:05:54.434 --> 00:05:56.501
So I was walking like this.
-And you're like --

00:05:56.501 --> 00:05:58.434
-I was just --
And then I was like, "No, no.

00:05:58.434 --> 00:05:59.901
It's absolutely fine.
I'm not in pain."

00:05:59.901 --> 00:06:01.634
-Yeah, everybody's like --
They're like,

00:06:01.634 --> 00:06:03.000
"Rina, why are you doing this?"

00:06:03.000 --> 00:06:04.634
-Your spine
is literally like this.

00:06:04.634 --> 00:06:06.067
-Oh, my gosh.
-Yeah.

00:06:06.067 --> 00:06:07.901
And then they were like,
"You need to go get some help."

00:06:07.901 --> 00:06:09.300
-Wow.
-Yeah.

00:06:09.300 --> 00:06:11.834
-And then, by the end of it,
did you get so into it?

00:06:11.834 --> 00:06:13.467
You're like, "Oh.
This is my second calling.

00:06:13.467 --> 00:06:14.767
Now I want to get into like..."

00:06:14.767 --> 00:06:16.334
-I would love to do more.
-You would?

00:06:16.334 --> 00:06:18.000
-I would love to do -- It's the
hardest thing I've ever done,

00:06:18.000 --> 00:06:19.300
but I would love to do more.

00:06:19.300 --> 00:06:21.067
-You couldn't have
crushed it harder, bud.

00:06:21.067 --> 00:06:22.167
-Thank you.

00:06:22.167 --> 00:06:23.234
-Couldn't have
crushed it harder.

00:06:23.234 --> 00:06:24.734
-Thank you.
-Well, well, well done.

00:06:24.734 --> 00:06:27.267
-Thank you.
-How do we set up what

00:06:27.267 --> 00:06:30.167
the movie's about without
spoiling "John Wick: Chapter 4"?

00:06:30.167 --> 00:06:32.000
-This is --
This is the weird thing about

00:06:32.000 --> 00:06:33.567
promoting a movie
versus promoting music.

00:06:33.567 --> 00:06:35.267
-Yeah, because
you can talk about the music.

00:06:35.267 --> 00:06:36.734
-Because you can talk
about the music.

00:06:36.734 --> 00:06:38.067
You can't talk about a movie.
-Yeah.

00:06:38.067 --> 00:06:39.701
-So, of course, I'm like --
Am I spoiling?

00:06:39.701 --> 00:06:42.934
Okay, but -- my character --

00:06:42.934 --> 00:06:44.267
-[ Imitates buzzer ]
-Right!

00:06:44.267 --> 00:06:45.634
-No, you can't say that.
-No, that's --

00:06:45.634 --> 00:06:47.567
-Can't say that.
-Lionsgate...I'm gone.

00:06:47.567 --> 00:06:49.200
-Let's try it a different way.
-Yeah.

00:06:49.200 --> 00:06:51.033
-Well, I think we're allowed
to say what John is doing.

00:06:51.033 --> 00:06:53.634
John is trying to --
-John's killing more people.

00:06:53.634 --> 00:06:56.167
[ Laughter and applause ]
-In the first ten seconds.

00:06:56.234 --> 00:06:58.767
[ Cheers and applause ]
In the first ten seconds.

00:06:58.767 --> 00:07:01.167
There's -- There's nunchucks.

00:07:01.167 --> 00:07:03.434
There's throwing stars.
-A lot of that.

00:07:03.434 --> 00:07:05.267
-There's everything
you would never thought.

00:07:05.267 --> 00:07:06.834
You go, "Oh, my God."
There's horses.

00:07:06.834 --> 00:07:08.200
-Yeah.
-In the first ten --

00:07:08.200 --> 00:07:10.801
Horseback.
-All from one dead dog.

00:07:10.801 --> 00:07:12.868
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:07:12.868 --> 00:07:14.567
-All for one --
Don't mess with someone's dog.

00:07:14.567 --> 00:07:16.534
-That's true.
-Don't mess with someone's pet.

00:07:16.534 --> 00:07:18.200
-I get it. I've got a dog.
-Yeah.

00:07:18.200 --> 00:07:19.567
-I totally get it.
-Don't mess with that.

00:07:19.567 --> 00:07:20.734
Yeah, that's -- Yeah, exactly.

00:07:20.734 --> 00:07:21.934
That's the best way
to set it up.

00:07:21.934 --> 00:07:23.100
-Yeah.
-Don't mess with someone's dog.

00:07:23.100 --> 00:07:24.567
-Yeah.
-I want to show a clip.

00:07:24.567 --> 00:07:27.234
Here's Rina Sawayama
in "John Wick: Chapter 4."

00:07:27.234 --> 00:07:29.267
Take a look.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:32.033 --> 00:07:35.400
-If they find you here,
the Table will kill my father.

00:07:35.400 --> 00:07:38.067
Me. Everyone.

00:07:38.067 --> 00:07:41.334
Because you broke the rules.

00:07:41.334 --> 00:07:42.834
You shouldn't have come.

00:07:42.834 --> 00:07:49.467
♪♪

00:07:49.467 --> 00:07:56.033
♪♪

00:07:59.834 --> 00:08:07.200
♪♪

00:08:07.200 --> 00:08:08.367
You armed?

00:08:09.767 --> 00:08:12.100
-Yeah! Are you kidding me?!

00:08:12.100 --> 00:08:14.534
[ Cheers and applause ]
Rina Sawayama!

00:08:14.534 --> 00:08:18.634
"John Wick: Chapter 4" is in
theaters and IMAX March 24th.

00:08:18.634 --> 00:08:21.000
We'll be right back with
stand-up from Nore Davis.

00:08:21.000 --> 00:08:22.300
Stick around, everybody.

